rica.com/stories/202510160154.html","title":"African Union suspends Madagascar from its organs and all activities","title_original":"Afrique: L'Union africaine suspend Madagascar de ses instances ainsi que de toutes ses activités","lang":"fr","publisher":"allAfrica","date":"2025-10-16","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.lexpress.mg/2026/02/union-africaine-razanamahasoa-plaide-la.html","title":"African Union: Razanamahasoa pleads Madagascar's case","title_original":"UNION AFRICAINE - Razanamahasoa plaide la cause malgache","lang":"fr","publisher":"L'Express de Madagascar","date":"2026-02","tier":3}],"alignment":null},{"toward":"NGA","grade":"partner","trend":"stable","bond":"unknown","since":2004,"last_verified":"2026-10-16","confidence":"C","dataset":"reciprocal","stale":false,"note":"African Union has not written its reading of Nigeria; the atlas mirrors Nigeria's 'partner' reading as 'partner' at low confidence, on the same evidence. Bond and trend are not assessed from this side.","sources":[{"url":"https://au.int/en/member_states/countryprofiles2","title":"African Union - member states","publisher":"African Union","date":"2026-10-12","tier":1},{"url":"https://von.gov.ng/nigeria-takes-helm-of-au-peace-and-security-council/","title":"Nigeria takes helm of AU Peace and Security Council","publisher":"Voice of Nigeria","date":"2026","tier":3},{"url":"https://guardian.ng/news/nigeria/national/shettima-departs-abuja-for-2026-au-summit/","title":"Shettima departs Abuja for 2026 AU summit","publisher":"The Guardian (Nigeria)","date":"2026-02","tier":3}],"alignment":null},{"toward":"SDN","grade":"partner","trend":"stable","bond":"unknown","since":"2021-10","last_verified":"2026-10-12","confidence":"C","dataset":"reciprocal","stale":false,"note":"African Union has not written its reading of Sudan; the atlas mirrors Sudan's 'reluctant partner' reading as 'partner' at low confidence, on the same evidence. Bond and trend are not assessed from this side.","sources":[{"url":"https://www.peaceau.org/en/article/press-statement-of-the-1264th-meeting-of-the-peace-and-security-council-held-on-11-march-2025-on-the-situation-in-sudan","title":"Press statement of the 1264th meeting of the Peace and Security Council, held on 11 March 2025, on the situation in Sudan","publisher":"African Union Peace and Security Council","date":"2025-03-11","tier":1},{"url":"https://qna.org.qa/en/news/news-details?id=african-union-condemns-forming-new-parallel-government-in-sudan-calls-for-ceasefire&date=30/07/2025","title":"African Union condemns forming new parallel government in Sudan, calls for ceasefire","publisher":"Qatar News Agency (state agency, report of AU statement)","date":"2025-07-30","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/09/us-ties-sudanese-army-leaders-un-visa-ceasefire-plan-sources-say","title":"US ties Sudanese army leader's UN visa to ceasefire plan, sources say","publisher":"Reuters (via Al-Monitor)","date":"2026-09-22","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c20lwznegk4o","title":"Sudan slams Uganda for hosting leader of RSF paramilitary force","publisher":"BBC","date":"2026-02-22","tier":3}],"alignment":null}],"stances_toward":[{"toward":"org-au","grade":"partner","trend":"stable","bond":"affinity","since":"2000-10-10","last_verified":"2026-10-16","confidence":"B","note":"Partner through FOCAC: RMB 360bn (about USD 51bn) pledged at the ninth forum (Sep 2024: USD 29.6bn of credit, USD 11.2bn of assistance, 30 connectivity and 30 clean-energy projects, a million jobs) and zero tariffs on all lines for the 53 African states that recognise Beijing (Changsha, Jun 2025, Eswatini excluded). Africa is the continent where Beijing's 'modernisation' frame meets no rival offer of the same size, and where every state but one votes One China. Bond - affinity: the anti-colonial narrative and the vote.","sources":[{"url":"https://www.bu.edu/gdp/2024/10/15/back-in-action-the-ninth-forum-on-china-africa-cooperation-sees-renewed-relations-and-development-prospects","title":"Back in Action: the Ninth Forum on China-Africa Cooperation sees renewed relations and development prospects","publisher":"Boston University Global Development Policy Center","date":"2024-10-15","tier":2},{"url":"https://cnbcafrica.com/2024/china-offers-africa-51-bln-in-fresh-funding-promises-a-million-jobs","title":"China offers Africa $51 bln in fresh funding, promises a million jobs","publisher":"CNBC Africa (Reuters)","date":"2024-09-05","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.spglobal.com/commodity-insights/en/news-research/latest-news/agriculture/061225-china-offers-zero-tariffs-to-53-african-nations-amid-us-trade-tensions","title":"China offers zero tariffs to 53 African nations amid US trade tensions","publisher":"S&P Global Commodity Insights","date":"2025-06-12","tier":3}],"stale":false,"alignment":null,"actor":"CHN"},{"toward":"org-au","grade":"reluctant_partner","trend":"stable","bond":"none","since":"2025-10","last_verified":"2026-10-16","confidence":"C","note":"The AU Peace and Security Council suspended Madagascar from all its activities and organs on 15 October 2025, after the military takeover. Madagascar answers by pleading its case rather than leaving: Malagasy press reported in February 2026 that it was pleading for its return, while the military leader denies the takeover was a coup. Reluctant partner is our reading of cooperation under necessity with visible contest over the verdict; no source uses the phrase. Trend stable: the suspension was still reported in late July 2026 search excerpts (those pages were not opened), so no change is sourced. Bond none is our reading. Gap: the PSC communiqué text was not opened in this pass; the AU card is a stub, so nothing is mirrored.","sources":[{"url":"https://fr.allafrica.com/stories/202510160154.html","title":"African Union suspends Madagascar from its organs and all activities","title_original":"Afrique: L'Union africaine suspend Madagascar de ses instances ainsi que de toutes ses activités","lang":"fr","publisher":"allAfrica","date":"2025-10-16","tier":3},{"url":"https://www.lexpress.mg/2026/02/union-africaine-razanamahasoa-plaide-la.html","title":"African Union: Razanamahasoa pleads Madagascar's case","title_original":"UNION AFRICAINE - Razanamahasoa plaide la cause malgache","lang":"fr","publisher":"L'Express de Madagascar","date":"2026-02","tier":3}],"stale":false,"alignment":null,"actor":"MDG"},{"toward":"org-au","grade":"partner","trend":"stable","bond":"affinity","since":2004,"last_verified":"2026-10-16","confidence":"B","note":"The stage on which Nigeria claims the lead. Member (AU list, tier 1); the only AU member with continuous membership of the Peace and Security Council since its creation in 2004, chair of the Council in May 2026, the first time since December 2022 (Voice of Nigeria); the 2026 summit in Addis Ababa was attended by Vice President Shettima, not Tinubu. A win in February 2026 on the Executive Council: a permanent seat on the board of the African Central Bank. The AU is also the arena of the South Africa contest (see ZAF). Partner rather than ally: no defence clause. Bond affinity: Pan-African identity, our reading. Some of the pages seen carried dates that did not match their content; the PSC chairmanship and the summit attendance should be checked against the AU site.","sources":[{"url":"https://au.int/en/member_states/countryprofiles2","title":"African Union - member states","publisher":"African Union","date":"2026-10-12","tier":1},{"url":"https://von.gov.ng/nigeria-takes-helm-of-au-peace-and-security-council/","title":"Nigeria takes helm of AU Peace and Security Council","publisher":"Voice of Nigeria","date":"2026","tier":3},{"url":"https://guardian.ng/news/nigeria/national/shettima-departs-abuja-for-2026-au-summit/","title":"Shettima departs Abuja for 2026 AU summit","publisher":"The Guardian (Nigeria)","date":"2026-02","tier":3}],"stale":false,"alignment":null,"actor":"NGA"},{"toward":"org-au","gra